  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kambampati. Galeswara Rao, vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh, on 22 July, 2021 The Hon'Ble Smt. Justice Lalitha Kanneganti Criminal Petition No. 3932 Of 2021 Order:",
    "facts": "The case of prosecution is that a report was lodged wherein it is alleged that on 25.02.2020 on receiving credible information S.I. of Police, N.Sagar Police Station along with his staff proceeded to T road junction Police Check Post and while they were conducting vehicle check, they stopped one Ashok Leyland Mini Truck bearing No.TS 12 UC 6892 which was coming from Hyderabad and found three persons. On checking the vehicle the Police found 1) Blue Bull Khaini sachets -28,080, 2) Miraj Khaini Sachets-12,000, 3) Khaleja sachets-17,040, 4) Rani Gutka sachets -39,000, 5) A1 tobacco sachets-16,000, 6) 900 grams of ganja. Police seized the said packets under the cover of a mediators report. Basing on the said report, the present crime is registered in which, the petitioner is arrayed as A9. 3.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that this Court had clearly held that this Court has clearly observed in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch that tobacco does not fall within the definition of \"food\" as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the FSS Act and possession or transportation of tobacco products will not constitute offences under Sections of IPC and FSS Act. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that petitioner is no way concerned with any of the allegations levelled in the complaint. He submits that this Court has granted pre-arrest bail to A3 and A7 order dated 23.09.2020 passed in Crl.P.No.3902 of 2020.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that this Court had clearly held that this Court has clearly observed in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch that tobacco does not fall within the definition of \"food\" as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the FSS Act and possession or transportation of tobacco products will not constitute offences under Sections of IPC and FSS Act. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that petitioner is no way concerned with any of the allegations levelled in the complaint.",
    "respondent_arguments": "He submits that this Court has granted pre-arrest bail to A3 and A7 order dated 23.09.2020 passed in Crl.P.No.3902 of 2020.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
